From: mothershipOS
Subject: [PATCH] bus: mhi: host: pci_generic: SDX55 inside a phone (fusion)

The SDX55 of an SM8250 phone has no flash: the host pushes sbl1 over BHI and serves the rest of its boot chain over
Sahara (mhi_sahara). Its subsystem ID (17cb:010c) is that of a Foxconn card; a "qcom,ext-sdx55m" compatible on
the modem's PCI device node selects a profile with sbl1, the stock firmware's channel map (Sahara, boot log, EFS,
DIAG, QMI, IPCR, DUN, IP_HW0), the control and bandwidth rings on MSI vector 0 with polling, the MSI doorbell
mapped into the modem's IOMMU domain, answered bandwidth requests and the M3 cycle at mission mode, without runtime suspend (the link does not come back). The SBL boot
log goes to the kernel log. After the alioth bring-up (github.com/cancelledbit/alioth-modem, GPL-2.0).

